course: dictionary
lesson: 12118
title: Colored: one word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Colored is an adjective when it describes a thing. It tells you the thing has a color, which means it is not plain white or black. «The colored lights glowed on the stage.» The lights are not white or black, so colored describes them.
explain: Colored is also the past of the verb color, which means to fill in with color, like with crayons. «Yesterday Mia colored the whole rainbow in.» Mia filled in the rainbow, so colored here is a verb about something that already happened.
explain: To tell which job it does, ask: is it describing a thing, or is someone doing an action in the past? Then try swapping in filled in. If the sentence still makes sense, colored is the verb.
fact: Colored means having a color, or not plain white or black.
fact: As a verb, colored is the past of color: it means filled in with color.
fact: Colored is the American spelling. The British spelling is coloured, with a u, and it means the same.
fact: «Colored pencils» are pencils with color in them, used for drawing and art.
fact: In maths, a shape's fraction can be the colored parts out of all the parts: 3 colored parts out of 4 is 3/4.
exercise: «The colored lights glowed on the stage.» What does colored mean here? | Very bright and loud | Filled in with crayons yesterday | *Having a color, not plain white or black | Broken or cracked
exercise: «Yesterday Mia colored the whole rainbow in.» What kind of word is colored here? | *A verb in the past: filled in with color | A noun for a type of paint | An adjective: having a color
exercise: Ben writes «coloured» with a u, and Sam writes «colored» without it. Who is right? | Only Sam, because the u is a mistake | Only Ben, because the u is always needed | *Both are right: one is British spelling and one is American spelling
test: «Lee colored the sun yellow.» What does colored mean in this sentence? | Very hot | Having a color, not plain white | Wet from the rain | *Filled in with color
test: Which sentence uses colored as an adjective? | «He will color the picture later.» | «She colored the map with green.» | *«The colored glass glittered in the sun.»
exam: In maths, 3 of the 4 equal parts of a shape are colored, so what fraction is colored? | *3/4 | 1/4 | 3/3 | 4/3
